# PX4 v1.16.2 external-vision parameters for GeoAnchor.
#
# The ArduPilot equivalent is the extnav.parm block in the configs/flight.yaml
# header. These are NOT translations of it -- the two firmwares expose a
# different set of knobs, and three of these have no ArduPilot counterpart at
# all. Every value below was read out of PX4's own parameter metadata
# (src/modules/ekf2/params_external_vision.yaml, params_gnss.yaml, module.yaml)
# for v1.16.2, not from a wiki page.
#
# Applied by scripts/px4_sitl.sh, which then reboots -- two of them say
# reboot_required in the metadata and are silently ignored until you do.
#
# name              value   why
EKF2_EV_CTRL            1   # bitmask, bit 0 = horizontal position ONLY.
                            # Bit 1 (vertical) stays clear: altitude is the
                            # flight controller's, from baro. Bit 2 (velocity)
                            # stays clear: this pipeline sends none. Bit 3
                            # (yaw) stays clear: it sends an identity
                            # quaternion, so claiming yaw would feed the
                            # estimator a constant heading of zero.
                            # DEFAULTS TO 0 -- external vision is OFF until this
                            # is set, which is the single most likely reason a
                            # perfectly good fix appears to do nothing.
EKF2_EV_NOISE_MD        0   # 0 = use the variance in OUR message, with
                            # EKF2_EVP_NOISE as a lower bound. 1 discards it
                            # and applies the parameter to every fix, which is
                            # the "trust every fix identically" behaviour this
                            # project's covariance work exists to avoid. If
                            # this is 1, nothing upstream of it matters.
EKF2_EVP_NOISE       0.05   # lower bound on our position sigma, metres. Set
                            # below the tightest sigma the estimator is
                            # expected to emit; anything tighter is silently
                            # raised to this. There is NO upper clamp on this
                            # path, unlike ArduPilot's [0.01, 100] m -- so a
                            # learned estimator has more range here, not less.
EKF2_EVP_GATE         5.0   # innovation gate, standard deviations. The same
                            # 5-sigma test EKF3 applies.
EKF2_EV_DELAY        50.0   # ms. REBOOT REQUIRED. Placeholder, matching the
                            # ArduPilot block; replace with YOUR measured
                            # median. Range here is 0-300, where ArduPilot's
                            # VISO_DELAY_MS stops at 250.
EKF2_EV_QMIN            0   # minimum ODOMETRY quality accepted, 0-100. 0
                            # accepts anything. The analogue of VISO_QUAL_MIN;
                            # raise it once inlier counts on the real
                            # reference are known.
EKF2_EV_POS_X         0.0   # camera offset forward of the IMU, metres
EKF2_EV_POS_Y         0.0   # right
EKF2_EV_POS_Z         0.0   # below
EKF2_HGT_REF            0   # 0 = baro. REBOOT REQUIRED. DEFAULTS TO 1 (GPS),
                            # which is the wrong reference for a vehicle that
                            # is about to have GNSS taken away. 3 (vision)
                            # would claim an altitude this pipeline does not
                            # produce.
